that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `native_decide` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `100` cells times
the `648` group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

def vdsrch10R4060 : Array Nat := #[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1]

def vsrch10R4060 : Magma.tup10R406 :=
  ⟨fun i ↦ ⟨vdsrch10R4060[i.1]! % 10, Nat.mod_lt _ (by decide)⟩, by native_decide⟩

